 "id": "forearm-servo-link-fdm",
 "brief": "Forearm link for my GRIP arm, carbon-fibre nylon (PA-CF) on an FDM printer, printed flat (layers\nalong +Z). One end screws onto the elbow servo's 25 mm aluminium disc horn: the horn's top face is\nz = 0 with its axis along Z through the origin, and the link sits on it with a solid 25 mm, 4 mm\nthick pad (z = 0 to 4) held by four M3 socket-head screws on a 20 mm circle at (10, 0), (0, 10),\n(-10, 0) and (0, -10), going down through 3.4 mm holes into the horn. Each head bears on top of\nthe pad and needs an 8 mm column clear above it for the hex key, and the horn's own centre screw\nneeds a 7 mm hole straight through the link over it. The other end, 100 mm along +X, holds a 608\nbearing (22 mm OD, 7 mm wide) with its axis along Z at (100, 0): seat z = 0 to 7 with at least 3\nmm of wall, pressed in from below, and the wrist shaft passes right through (10 mm hole). The link\nfits in x = -16 to 116, y = -16 to 16, z = 0 to 14. The elbow servo is a DS3225 (stall torque 2.5\nN.m about Z) and can stall with the far end blocked; the wrist and payload are 0.8 kg on a fast\narm (design for 2 g), pulling the bearing along -Y with their centre of mass 30 mm below the link\n(on the bearing axis at z = -30); and the bearing end can take a 10 N knock along -Z. Safety\nfactor 2, the bearing end may move at most 0.6 mm under any of these, and under 21 g.",
 "attachments": [],
